Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:42:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 5, patch 3;
 built on a35fd4bce with the ten patches of series 4 and the first two of
 series 5 applied): THE DAY IS ONE DAY, AND ITS GUARD READS EVERY COMMIT
 (Review 79, the second reader's row 10, its first and second parts; the first
 reader's R79-SM-47). The day a gate judges by was the day the commit states,
 in the commit's own zone. The guard on that day read the commit's time. A
 commit made one second after its parent and stated in a zone twelve hours
 behind, after a parent stated fourteen hours ahead, passed the guard and
 moved the day two days back. And the guard read main's own line only: a
 commit dated before its parent on a branch that is then merged, and a merge
 dated before the branch it merges, were not read. THE MEND: every day a gate
 or a debt checker takes from a commit is the day, in UTC, of the commit's
 time, in the one module that decides the day, in the gates, in the checker of
 leads and in the date of a review's anchor; so the day and its guard read one
 clock, and where the guard holds the day does not go back. The guard reads
 every commit that the head reaches and its root does not, each beside each of
 its parents. WHAT MOVES ON MAIN: of the 38 commits after the rule's root,
 three were made in the first hour after midnight in main's zone, and their
 day is now the day before; at main's head nothing moves. On main no commit
 after the root is dated before a parent, on any line: there is no other line
 after the root. The comment in the relay checker that said the day cannot
 stand still says what the guard bounds: a run of commits each dated at its
 parent's time keeps the day still. That is a comment, and it has no test.
 Four lines of the first series' lock that read the day as the commit states
 it now read it as the gates do, each with a dated note. What it does not
 reach: between a parent's time and the real time a commit's time is its
 maker's to choose, as before. The lock: two tests added to
 tests/test_gates_are_a_function_of_the_commit.py. On the commit before, both
 fail: the day of a commit made a second after its parent is two days earlier
 and the guard passes; and a commit dated a month before its parent, merged
 from a branch, is read by nothing. Tested against planted errors; computed
 once. 0 of 19.

